  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "There are 3 bad oranges and 7 good oranges. $\\therefore \\quad X=$ number of bad oranges drawn.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a1LXvsdOljerU8qA0xMcoSupG5Jos_kNLAO6k9UPwbs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\therefore$ Variance\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =0^2 \\cdot \\frac{{ }^7 C_2}{{ }^{10} C_2}+1^2 \\cdot\\left(\\frac{3 \\times 7}{{ }^{10} C_2}\\right)+2^2\\left(\\frac{3}{{ }^{10} C_2}\\right) \\\\\n& \\quad-\\left(0+1 \\cdot \\frac{3 \\times 7}{{ }^{10} C_2}+2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{{ }^{10} C_2}\\right)^2 \\\\\n& =\\frac{28}{75}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
